# Responsive Design Baseline

## Design Preset

**Desktop fullscreen (large viewport) is the canonical design.** The current desktop layout and styling are the source of truth.

## Constraint

When adding or adjusting responsive behavior:

- **Desktop design stays unchanged** — Do not modify styles that affect the desktop fullscreen view
- **Add breakpoints only for smaller viewports** — Use `md:`, `sm:`, `max-md:`, etc. to adapt for tablet and mobile
- **Mobile-first overrides only** — New responsive rules should apply at smaller breakpoints; desktop inherits the existing (unmodified) styles

## Breakpoint Strategy

- Default / base styles = desktop fullscreen (preserve as-is)
- `md:` and below = tablet
- `sm:` and below = mobile

Do not add `lg:` or `xl:` overrides that change the current desktop appearance.

## Layout Preservation

- **Never stack elements that are side-by-side on desktop.** Use proportional scaling instead.
- Keep the same grid columns (e.g. grid-cols-6, grid-cols-3) at all viewport sizes.
- Scale element sizes (width, padding, font) responsively so the layout fits; do not change to flex-col or reduce grid-cols on smaller screens.
